        "original_id": "01c6a4e1-9823-54dd-83d5-7bac88e9a4c1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Teams: Hawaii Warriors, Houston Cougars, Boise State Broncos, Oregon State Beavers\n- People: June Jones\n- Organizations: University of Hawaii at Manoa, Hamilton Tiger-Cats, Canadian Football League\n- Events: 2003 NCAA Division I-A football season, 2003 Sheraton Hawaii Bowl, 2013 Hawaii Bowl\n\nFacts:\n- In the 2003 NCAA Division I-A football season, the 2003 Hawaii Warriors football team represented the University of Hawaii at Manoa.\n- In 2003, the Hawaii Warriors completed their second straight winning season and their fourth winning season in five years under head coach June Jones, ending the year with a bowl win.\n- The 2003 Sheraton Hawaii Bowl matched the hometown Hawaii Warriors against the Houston Cougars.\n- June Jones, born February 19, 1953, is an American football coach and former player.\n- June Jones has served as head coach of the Hamilton Tiger-Cats of the Canadian Football League.\n- The 2013 Hawaii Bowl was the twelfth edition of the Hawaii Bowl and featured the Boise State Broncos of the Mountain West Conference against the Oregon State Beavers of the Pac-12 Conference.",
